    "turn_text": "it's against California. They've passed legislation, several pieces of legislation in last year, basically, that says to the federal ICE officers, actually direct employers, for example, in California not to allow ICE officers voluntarily own their property. And then if they come to their property, they must notify the employees in advance that the ICE is coming, presumably so they can flee. They bar the kind of routine cooperative communications that exist by far throughout the country between ICE officers or immigration officers and state officers. They create a situation in which people who are arrested in California, who are illegally here, and then you have committed in addition serious crimes they don't allow the uh... federal i-th officers to pick them up in the jail after they've been detained by california they released them into the community that our people have to go out and find them much much much much more dangerous for our officers for citizens for children who may be in the way",
